| 400, 650, 1000\nFMR-Dual: 250, 400 | 400, 650, 1000 | 650, 1000\n\nqmin:\nFMR: 0.25 ×4 | 0.25 ×4 | 0.25 ×4 | 0.2 ×4, 0.4 | 0.4 ×4 | 0.6 ×3 | 0.6 ×4 | 1, 1, 2.5 | 1.6 ×3 | 2.5, 2.5, 6.25\nFMR-Dual: 1, 2.5 | 2.5, 4, 4 | 4, 6.5\n\nqt:\nFMR: 0.5, 0.8, 1.25, 2 | 0.8, 1.25, 2, 3.2 | 1.25, 2, 3.2, 5 | 1.25, 2, 3.2, 5, 8 | 3.2, 5, 8, 12.5 | 5, 8, 12.5 | 5, 8, 12.5, 20 | 8, 12.5, 20 | 12.5, 20, 32 | 20, 32, 50\nFMR-Dual: 12.5, 20 | 20, 32, 32 | 32, 50\n\nmaximum_pressure (bar):\nFMR: 101 ×4 | 101 ×4 | 101 ×4 | 101 ×4, 12 | 101 ×3, 12 | 101 ×3 | 101 ×3, 12 | 101 ×3 | 101 ×3, 12 | 101 ×2, 12\nFMR-Dual: 21, 21 | 21, 21, 12 | 21, 21\n\naccuracy_class:\nFMR: 1.0 ×3, then \"1.0 or 1.5\" for G25; 1.0, 1.0, \"1.0 or 1.5\", \"1.0 or 1.5\"; 1.0, \"1.0 or 1.5\" ×3; \"1.0 or 1.5\" ×4, 1.0 for G16@0.73... \n\nLet me list carefully:\n1. G6 V0.25: \"1.0\"\n2. G10 V0.25: \"1.0\"\n3. G16 V0.25: \"1.0\"\n4. G25 V0.25: \"1.0 or 1.5\"\n5. G10 V0.39: \"1.0\"\n6. G16 V0.39: \"1.0\"\n7. G25 V0.39: \"1.0 or 1.5\"\n8. G40 V0.39: \"1.0 or 1.5\"\n9. G16 V0.61: \"1.0\"\n10. G25 V0.61: \"1.0 or 1.5\"\n11. G40 V0.61: \"1.0 or 1.5\"\n12. G65 V0.61: \"1.0 or 1.5\"\n13. G16 V0.73: \"1.0\"\n14. G25 V0.73: \"1.0 or 1.5\"\n15. G40 V0.73: \"1.0 or 1.5\"\n16. G65 V0.73: \"1.0 or 1.5\"\n17. G100 V0.73: \"1.0 or 1.5\"\n18-37: \"1.0 or 1.5\"\nFMR-Dual: all \"1.0 or 1.5\"\n\nOK. Now write the matrix table rows fully.\n\nTable 2 rows (as objects):\n{\"cyclic_volume\": 0.25, \"g_value\": \"G6\", \"qmax\": 10, \"qmin\": 0.25, \"qt\": 0.5, \"maximum_pressure\": 101, \"connection_diameter\": \"Threaded\", \"transfer_relationship_revolutions\": 4004.325, \"accuracy_class\": \"1.0\"}\n... etc as enumerated.\n\nTable 3 rows:\n{\"cyclic_volume\": 2.41, \"g_value\": \"G160\", \"qmax\": 250, \"qmin\": 1, \"qt\": 12.5, \"maximum_pressure\": 21, \"connection_diameter\": \"80 or 100\", \"transfer_relationship_revolutions\": 414.462, \"accuracy_class\": \"1.0 or 1.5\"}\n{\"cyclic_volume\": 2.41, \"g_value\": \"G250\", \"qmax\": 400, \"qmin\": 2.5, \"qt\": 20, \"maximum_pressure\": 21, \"connection_diameter\": \"80 or 100\", \"transfer_relationship_revolutions\": 414.462, \"accuracy_class\": \"1.0 or 1.5\"}\n{\"cyclic_volume\": 3.96, \"g_value\": \"G250\", \"qmax\": 400, \"qmin\": 2.5, \"qt\": 20, \"maximum_pressure\": 21, \"connection_diameter\": \"100 or 150\", \"transfer_relationship_revolutions\": 252.282, \"accuracy_class\": \"1.0 or 1.5\"}\n{\"cyclic_volume\": 3.96, \"g_value\": \"G400\", \"qmax\": 650, \"qmin\": 4, \"qt\": 32, \"maximum_pressure\": 21, \"connection_diameter\": \"100 or 150\", \"transfer_relationship_revolutions\": 252.282, \"accuracy_class\": \"1.0 or 1.5\"}\n{\"cyclic_volume\": 3.96, \"g_value\": \"G650\", \"qmax\": 1000, \"qmin\": 4, \"qt\": 32, \"maximum_pressure\": 12, \"connection_diameter\": \"150 or 200\", \"transfer_relationship_revolutions\": 252.282, \"accuracy_class\": \"1.0 or 1.5\"}\n{\"cyclic_volume\": 6.34, \"g_value\": \"G400\", \"qmax\": 650, \"qmin\": 4, \"qt\": 32, \"maximum_pressure\": 21, \"connection_diameter\": \"150 or 200\", \"transfer_relationship_revolutions\": 157.676, \"accuracy_class\": \"1.0 or 1.5\"}\n{\"cyclic_volume\": 6.34, \"g_value\": \"G650\", \"qmax\": 1000, \"qmin\": 6.5, \"qt\": 50, \"maximum_pressure\": 21, \"connection_diameter\": \"150 or 200\", \"transfer_relationship_revolutions\": 157.676, \"accuracy_class\": \"1.0 or 1.5\"}\n\nDrums table:\n{\"meter_size\": \"G6\", \"min_drums_before_comma\": 5, \"min_drums_behind_comma\": 3, \"control_element_m3\": 0.0002}\n{\"meter_size\": \"G10 - G65\", \"min_drums_before_comma\": 6, \"min_drums_behind_comma\": 2, \"control_element_m3\": 0.002}\n{\"meter_size\": \"G100 - G650\", \"min_drums_before_comma\": 7, \"min_drums_behind_comma\": 1, \"control_element_m3\": 0.02}\n\nName: \"Minimum number of drums and control element per meter size\".\n\nDescription for drums table: \"For the name plate cyclic volume display: minimum number of drums before/behind the comma and the control element value, by meter size. The second drum column header was blank in the source; values correspond to digits behind the comma.\"\n\nOK, now output. It'll be long but that's required. Let me be careful with decimals: European commas converted (4004,325 → 4004.325, 0,25 → 0.25, etc.).\n\nAccuracy classes in recommendation: [1, 1.5]. In JSON, 1.0 renders as 1.0. Fine.\n\nNow double-check date_issued: 30 January 2015 → \"2015-01-30\". Test report same date.\n\nAlso the header on page 1: \"Number R137/2012-NL1-15.01\" — good.\n\nWrite final JSON now. Ensure valid JSON, no trailing commas, no markdown fences.",
